Feature: MAVLink network
  Pilots who share a [[MAVLink]] network see each other's planes. Each plane sends its
  position a few times a second. The network has a longer range than Remote ID.

  Expectation: A plane on the MAVLink network gets a marker
    Given the other plane is sending MAVLink
    And the distance to the other plane is at most 2000 m
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 1 other plane
    And the marker of the other plane is live
    And the source of the marker is MAVLink

  Expectation: The MAVLink network has a limit too
    Given the other plane is sending MAVLink
    And the distance to the other plane is at least 6000 m
    And the map has 0 other planes
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 0 other planes

  Expectation: A plane that sends both gets one marker
    Remote ID and MAVLink tell the station about the same plane. The station joins the two
    when they are at the same place. The label of the marker names both sources.
    Given the other plane is sending both
    And the distance to the other plane is at most 500 m
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 1 other plane
    And the source of the marker is Remote ID and MAVLink
